From 7944d7ff6f12292966e0d062af6f57461ea5c074 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 19:02:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0209 -- #31 v1.0.8 audio-delivery: deferred organya PCM
 cache

Freeze-avoidance self-heal (team-lead-directed). A mid-gameplay <CMU that fell
back to live synth (cache miss outside the post-load window, patch 0206) is
recorded in a 1-deep pending slot; at the NEXT load_stage the song is rendered
to its CACHE\<NAME>.PCM during the load pause (phase=load_stage), so a later
re-encounter is an instant cache HIT (real-time, no freeze). Net: a boss/event
song is slow-not-frozen on its FIRST encounter, then self-heals to real-time
after the next load -- and NEVER a mid-gameplay freeze.

The deferred render uses a TEMP Song + a LOCAL buffer -- it never touches the
active playback buffer (g_org_prerender_buf). A header-only _org_cache_valid
probe skips an already-cached song without clobbering the active buffer.
Reuses 0206's _org_render_song + 0208's _org_cache_store. map.cpp drains the
slot in the load_stage phase guard window (cache write is load-band). No-op
when the slot is empty or pre-render is killswitched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/map.cpp           |  9 ++++++
 src/sound/Organya.cpp | 72 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 80 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

